  "conclusion": "In 10 languages, with no server the field kept the focus in 20 of 20 samples and its value grew under typing. With the control connected and idle it lost the focus in 19 of the 19 samples that ran; 1 did not run, because a text field kept the focus through the settle step's three Escapes after the control sample before it. With the candidate it kept the focus in 20 of 20 and its value grew. Every server sample that ran had its six subscriptions accepted and sent between 4 and 6 notifications before the rename opened.",
  "limits": [
    "The rename was opened through Track > Rename Track, not by double-clicking the name, and the typing was under 2-Set Korean, not ABC.",
    "When editing begins mid-cycle the candidate stops at the next read, and during the track walk before the next help read; one help read already under way runs to its end. Whether a sample began mid-cycle was not read, so that path rests on the unit tests.",
    "One Logic installation and one fixture; the fixture's poll cycle is short, unlike the 74-track project where a 12.6 s median was measured.",
    "The control is the 086821fd tree with main's poller, not a commit of its own; main's poller does not compile against this head's publication interface.",
    "The run was made at 711bfc98 with the candidate built at 13521f0f; the commits between change only the probe.",
    "Whether a yield came at the document-path query, inside a header before its help reads, at the publication or between resource reads was not read in this run; those paths rest on the unit tests and their mutants.",
    "The subscribed client never read a resource itself; it only received notifications."
